WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.030 --> 00:05.900
Physics.

3
00:05.900 --> 00:08.670
Whoa, finally! It's been way too long.

4
00:08.670 --> 00:10.430
I've picked all my universities.

5
00:10.430 --> 00:11.500
I kind of cheated on London.

6
00:11.500 --> 00:12.700
What made you change your mind?

7
00:12.700 --> 00:16.270
It's been so long. You were really cool back there, Din.

8
00:16.700 --> 00:17.700
Can I get a hug?

9
00:17.700 --> 00:19.230
I hope things go well for you, Yok.

10
00:19.230 --> 00:20.000
Okay.

11
00:20.000 --> 00:21.670
Come have moo kratha at my place.

12
00:25.230 --> 00:26.270
I can't peel shrimp.

13
00:26.270 --> 00:27.430
Just say so next time.

14
00:28.300 --> 00:29.230
I'll peel them for you.

15
00:29.900 --> 00:31.170
Thank you, Din.

16
00:31.170 --> 00:34.430
Why not clean the wound? At least put some ointment on it.

17
00:35.000 --> 00:36.900
Shift back a little.

18
00:36.900 --> 00:40.260
Welcome, everyone, to the 11th Science Smart Camp,

19
00:40.260 --> 00:41.400
officially.

20
00:41.400 --> 00:44.970
So let's start with... the first activity.

21
00:45.900 --> 00:48.270
And each group will have...

22
00:51.130 --> 00:53.570
Everyone, let's all listen to Star.

23
00:59.630 --> 01:01.830
If it's bothering you, shouldn't you make a decision?

24
01:01.830 --> 01:02.930
I'm scared of losing my friends.

25
01:02.930 --> 01:04.129
I'm the one who likes you.

26
01:04.129 --> 01:05.600
So it's on me to deal with my own feelings.

27
01:05.600 --> 01:07.500
The promise you made me when I was a kid,

28
01:07.500 --> 01:09.230
do you still remember it?

29
01:18.800 --> 01:21.400
Hey, everyone, help! Star fell in the water!

30
01:22.100 --> 01:24.130
The activity he came up with costs too much.

31
01:24.130 --> 01:25.670
And it definitely can't be family money.

32
01:25.670 --> 01:27.470
I already told you, I'll find a way.

33
01:27.470 --> 01:28.870
Change the singer. I'm asking you.

34
01:28.870 --> 01:31.700
And I still don't understand why you're picking a fight with me.

35
01:31.700 --> 01:33.300
He's someone who's always ready to cause trouble.

36
01:33.300 --> 01:34.900
Not here to lecture you. I'm here to help.

37
01:36.830 --> 01:38.070
Everyone, step outside.

38
01:38.270 --> 01:41.030
Star. Star, are you okay?

39
01:42.470 --> 01:43.900
Star, can you hear me?

40
01:48.870 --> 01:50.870
Satayu, sweetheart... Star.

41
02:11.730 --> 02:12.530
Satayu.

42
02:14.280 --> 02:15.070
Satayu.

43
02:15.070 --> 02:16.530
Ms. James. / Yes, dear.

44
02:17.630 --> 02:18.430
Din.

45
02:18.600 --> 02:19.400
How are you feeling?

46
02:37.800 --> 02:39.370
Are you okay, sweetheart? Can you sit up?

47
02:39.900 --> 02:42.570
I'm fine. Totally fine.

48
02:43.600 --> 02:47.100
You scared me half to death. You were out cold for a whole night.

49
02:47.100 --> 02:49.430
I'm sorry. / It's all right, it's all right.

50
02:50.000 --> 02:53.070
As long as you're okay, as long as you're safe, that's all that matters.

51
02:56.500 --> 02:58.470
Thank you too, Din.

52
03:01.530 --> 03:02.870
And the camp right now...

53
03:02.870 --> 03:05.830
Don't you worry about the camp.

54
03:05.830 --> 03:07.300
Take care of yourself first.

55
03:09.770 --> 03:10.770
You're sure you're okay?

56
03:11.670 --> 03:12.800
I'm okay.

57
03:13.600 --> 03:16.070
Phoodin, look after him.

58
03:23.030 --> 03:24.100
Star, you're sure?

59
03:25.270 --> 03:26.270
I'm okay, ma'am.

60
03:28.530 --> 03:29.770
Then if you're really okay,

61
03:29.770 --> 03:31.730
the camp activities carry on.

62
03:32.270 --> 03:34.870
But I mean it, look after each other, Phoodin.

63
03:34.870 --> 03:36.770
And don't let an accident like this happen again.

64
03:39.700 --> 03:40.930
Okay, okay.

65
03:42.670 --> 03:43.970
Thank you so much, teacher.

66
03:45.600 --> 03:47.770
Ow.

67
03:47.770 --> 03:49.870
What a relief for you all.

68
03:57.730 --> 03:59.070
Okay.

69
03:59.300 --> 04:00.830
Teu went down too.

70
04:00.830 --> 04:02.070
Teu got himself a cut.

71
04:02.070 --> 04:03.670
So how are you?

72
04:03.670 --> 04:05.600
Okay, but it still hurts a bit.

73
04:07.470 --> 04:11.430
Shall we get back to the camp? See it through to the end.

74
04:11.430 --> 04:12.230
Let's do it!

75
07:04.430 --> 07:06.830
The promise you made me when I was a kid,

76
07:07.700 --> 07:09.430
do you still remember it?

77
07:30.470 --> 07:32.200
So what are you going to do now, huh?

78
07:32.200 --> 07:33.770
You went and talked to him like that.

79
07:33.770 --> 07:35.430
He was still stammering.

80
07:35.430 --> 07:37.130
I don't think so.

81
07:40.670 --> 07:43.430
I think... maybe I should just stop.

82
07:44.530 --> 07:45.330
Est.

83
07:45.730 --> 07:46.770
Let me borrow your phone.

84
07:46.770 --> 07:47.700
What for?

85
07:47.700 --> 07:48.870
Order some dog food.

86
07:48.870 --> 07:50.200
Whoa, that's the one.

87
07:50.770 --> 07:52.320
I bet we're getting another round, man.

88
07:52.330 --> 07:54.930
But I think... this time I'm serious.

89
07:55.400 --> 07:56.530
Ow.

90
07:56.530 --> 07:58.230
Hey, order some for me too.

91
07:58.770 --> 07:59.570
Which brand?

92
07:59.570 --> 08:01.130
Make it two, or I won't be full.

93
08:01.130 --> 08:02.600
Go for it, man.

94
08:02.600 --> 08:04.130
Are you even my friend?

95
08:12.030 --> 08:13.330
For real. / Seriously?

96
08:18.800 --> 08:20.530
Hey, Aof's here.

97
08:22.600 --> 08:24.770
Oh no. What do we do now?

98
08:26.470 --> 08:27.370
Are you going to talk to him?

99
08:28.030 --> 08:30.130
I... I'm not.

100
08:30.430 --> 08:31.630
I'm not ready.

101
08:48.900 --> 08:50.500
I think you should go home.

102
08:51.070 --> 08:53.830
My friend isn't feeling up to it.

103
08:53.830 --> 08:57.300
Yeah. Whichever way you came, go back the same way.

104
08:57.730 --> 08:59.370
You may be my idol,

105
09:00.130 --> 09:02.170
but I have to protect my friend.

106
09:05.400 --> 09:08.230
I think you should wait and talk tomorrow.

107
09:08.230 --> 09:10.130
If Chemi wants to talk, you'll get your chance.

108
09:10.130 --> 09:14.230
I can't. This is important.

109
09:14.770 --> 09:16.870
I don't want Chemi misunderstanding me.

110
09:25.070 --> 09:26.570
Could you all help me out?

111
09:29.470 --> 09:30.470
No.

112
09:30.970 --> 09:33.770
But promise us, if we help you this time,

113
09:34.300 --> 09:36.730
you'll do everything we ask.

114
09:36.800 --> 09:38.900
Everything, really?

115
09:39.200 --> 09:40.300
Zac.

116
09:43.830 --> 09:45.230
Then tell me this.

117
09:45.500 --> 09:48.100
Does saying that mean you already have an answer for my friend?

118
09:51.070 --> 09:54.630
Right. Isn't it that you have no answer at all,

119
09:54.630 --> 09:56.900
and you just came to test my friend's feelings?

120
09:59.500 --> 10:02.230
Then let us tell you...

121
10:02.770 --> 10:05.800
how our friend is doing, and what you should do now.

122
10:13.930 --> 10:15.830
My friend's doing just fine.

123
10:15.830 --> 10:17.300
You don't need to worry that much.

124
10:17.300 --> 10:19.270
So you can head home now.

125
10:20.470 --> 10:21.830
It's probably better for you.

126
10:24.730 --> 10:26.430
I think you should go.

127
10:29.270 --> 10:30.600
Chemi.

128
10:34.170 --> 10:36.370
I still want to talk to you, Chemi.

129
10:46.530 --> 10:48.230
Please just go home.

130
11:05.900 --> 11:09.770
Chemi, Aof's gone.

131
11:30.270 --> 11:31.900
I get you now.

132
13:14.100 --> 13:18.100
Then I'll hand it over to the M.4 juniors.

133
14:36.130 --> 14:38.830
Thank you. Thank you.

134
15:17.770 --> 15:18.570
What's bugging you?

135
15:21.900 --> 15:22.970
Nothing.

136
15:27.030 --> 15:29.130
You can talk to me about anything.

137
15:29.130 --> 15:30.770
I won't tell anyone.

138
15:31.170 --> 15:32.270
I promise.

139
15:36.370 --> 15:38.530
It's nothing really.

140
15:39.230 --> 15:41.400
I just haven't been feeling good about it.

141
15:44.430 --> 15:46.400
When Star fell in the water,

142
15:46.400 --> 15:48.130
all I could do was shout.

143
15:48.130 --> 15:50.470
I couldn't actually help him at all.

144
15:54.070 --> 15:56.900
But I think it was your shouting, Time,

145
15:59.700 --> 16:01.970
that let everyone know Star had fallen in.

146
16:11.730 --> 16:12.830
I'm hungry.

147
16:13.600 --> 16:15.000
Want to grab a bite together?

148
16:16.470 --> 16:18.570
No thanks. You go ahead.

149
17:00.030 --> 17:01.570
Think it over again.

150
17:05.000 --> 17:07.430
No thanks. You go ahead.

151
17:12.130 --> 17:14.400
But I'm worried it's too spicy.

152
17:14.970 --> 17:16.630
Time, can you taste it for me?

153
17:17.470 --> 17:20.099
If you're worried it's spicy, why not use half a packet?

154
17:20.430 --> 17:24.230
Come on, the makers already figured it out — this much is what tastes right.

155
17:25.200 --> 17:26.170
Just do it.

156
17:26.170 --> 17:27.700
Taste it for me, please.

157
17:58.200 --> 18:00.370
Not spicy. It's good.

158
18:00.930 --> 18:01.930
Really?

159
18:02.670 --> 18:04.900
But I think I took too few noodles just now.

160
18:05.170 --> 18:06.570
One more time?

161
18:12.900 --> 18:14.500
Then I'll have some.

162
18:25.200 --> 18:27.600
Not spicy at all. It's good.

163
18:29.270 --> 18:31.200
But if you're going to eat this much,

164
18:31.200 --> 18:32.430
why not just eat with me?

165
18:34.830 --> 18:37.670
Your stomach's that loud, why hold back?

166
18:38.730 --> 18:40.400
You heard that?

167
18:41.100 --> 18:42.570
Loud and clear.

168
18:44.100 --> 18:46.700
It's just, lately I feel so guilty.

169
18:46.700 --> 18:48.800
I study late, right?

170
18:48.800 --> 18:50.330
So I got into late-night eating.

171
18:50.330 --> 18:52.700
Before I knew it, my pants got tight.

172
18:52.700 --> 18:55.270
So I decided to quit eating late.

173
18:57.930 --> 19:00.300
It's fine. We'll start over tomorrow.

174
19:00.770 --> 19:02.570
If you're hungry today, you eat.

175
19:02.970 --> 19:05.030
I'm not making you eat alone, Time.

176
19:07.430 --> 19:10.670
I'll eat with you, so you don't have to feel guilty.

177
19:17.070 --> 19:18.830
You really are something.

178
19:19.630 --> 19:21.270
Fine, let's eat. Come on.

179
19:21.270 --> 19:22.770
Here, go ahead.

180
19:23.430 --> 19:24.800
Put it right here.

181
19:28.100 --> 19:29.930
I'll dig in.

182
19:40.130 --> 19:41.830
I'll dig in, then.

183
19:46.930 --> 19:48.200
Refreshing.

184
19:48.570 --> 19:49.770
Want a meatball?

185
19:50.170 --> 19:50.970
Here.

186
19:55.330 --> 19:57.900
Nice and big.

187
20:17.030 --> 20:18.130
Physics.

188
20:21.170 --> 20:23.130
So you're not going after him?

189
20:23.130 --> 20:24.530
If you think I'm him...

190
20:26.170 --> 20:28.330
He said he was just going to get water.

191
20:29.630 --> 20:30.930
By now the whole pond's probably gone.

192
20:31.670 --> 20:33.570
I saw him sitting over there like some music-video heartthrob.

193
20:33.570 --> 20:36.400
So why didn't you bring him back to the tent?

194
20:36.970 --> 20:39.830
You think if I went after him, he'd just come back with me?

195
20:40.330 --> 20:44.070
You think I'd walk in there and play the music-video heartthrob opposite him, like—

196
20:45.230 --> 20:47.730
Mr. Physics, I'm Fuen.

197
20:48.770 --> 20:51.030
Mr. Physics, would you come back to the tent with me?

198
20:51.030 --> 20:52.030
Please?

199
21:03.300 --> 21:05.830
Honestly, I just don't want to get involved with you two anymore.

200
21:06.230 --> 21:08.100
I can barely handle my own life.

201
21:10.600 --> 21:14.830
About Chemi, just talk to Physics straight.

202
21:15.800 --> 21:18.330
You're always so good at this when it's my problem.

203
21:18.330 --> 21:20.900
How about this: you and I go at the same time,

204
21:23.230 --> 21:25.070
and sit down and talk separately.

205
21:30.200 --> 21:31.800
I'm staying out of it.

206
21:35.170 --> 21:37.870
I mean... I don't even know what I'm supposed to do.

207
21:37.870 --> 21:40.470
By now I know that... I like him.

208
21:44.600 --> 21:45.900
But when he came and said to me,

209
21:47.300 --> 21:48.900
Do you still remember that day?

210
21:48.900 --> 21:50.430
it made me feel like...

211
21:50.800 --> 21:53.970
I don't know if he really likes me, or if he's just...

212
21:57.930 --> 21:59.730
hung up on what was said.

213
22:02.170 --> 22:05.130
Have you ever just asked him straight?

214
22:05.470 --> 22:07.300
And have you ever done that with Physics?

215
22:07.300 --> 22:09.170
Just come out and ask him.

216
22:15.570 --> 22:16.970
It's not the same.

217
22:17.800 --> 22:18.930
How is it not the same?

218
22:19.500 --> 22:22.600
Physics has made it so damn obvious he's liked you since M.2.

219
22:26.700 --> 22:30.530
I'm Physics. I just transferred here. Nice to meet you.

220
23:00.100 --> 23:00.800
M.2?

221
23:01.270 --> 23:03.730
Yeah, you idiot.

222
23:03.730 --> 23:05.000
You really had no idea?

223
23:07.030 --> 23:09.400
Since M.2. Think about it.

224
23:09.400 --> 23:11.800
He kept you and me apart like a monk and a woman — no touching allowed.

225
23:12.370 --> 23:14.670
Tang and I could barely even touch you.

226
23:22.530 --> 23:24.430
Does the power never go out at your place?

227
23:24.430 --> 23:25.900
Light a candle once in a while, Fuen.

228
23:32.130 --> 23:33.430
It's from me.

229
23:41.830 --> 23:43.470
Why'd you buy me candles?

230
23:45.730 --> 23:46.870
In case your power goes out.

231
23:47.830 --> 23:49.200
Light them right away.

232
23:53.530 --> 23:55.900
How much longer are you going to leave me standing in the sun?

233
23:55.900 --> 23:58.670
It's hot. Let's go to school. It's getting hot.

234
24:01.000 --> 24:01.870
Hurry.

235
24:57.700 --> 24:59.170
I'll be back, then.

236
25:35.770 --> 25:38.930
You'd sleep right here if I hadn't come, wouldn't you?

237
26:06.830 --> 26:08.430
If I hadn't come,

238
26:09.930 --> 26:11.930
you weren't going back to your room?

239
26:13.930 --> 26:14.730
Of course I was.

240
26:16.930 --> 26:18.730
I just wanted to give you space.

241
26:20.070 --> 26:21.600
After I told you that,

242
26:23.600 --> 26:25.730
you've been thinking about it all day, haven't you?

243
26:33.630 --> 26:35.300
I just found out from Aof

244
26:37.300 --> 26:38.000
that...

245
26:38.670 --> 26:40.400
you've liked me since M.2?

246
27:28.030 --> 27:29.670
How did you stand it?

247
27:50.600 --> 27:52.430
Because I like you so damn much.

248
28:00.600 --> 28:02.270
I don't know...

249
28:04.670 --> 28:07.230
what you're like when you like someone.

250
28:14.070 --> 28:15.370
But for me,

251
28:28.900 --> 28:31.200
I never saw you as just a friend to begin with.

252
28:40.970 --> 28:43.730
I'm scared, Physics.

253
28:53.530 --> 28:56.300
I'm scared that if I cross that line,

254
28:58.230 --> 29:00.700
and I lose the best friend I have in you,

255
29:03.430 --> 29:05.170
I couldn't take it.

256
29:32.000 --> 29:32.730
I understand.

257
29:36.500 --> 29:38.370
It's okay. I can wait.

258
29:44.930 --> 29:51.900
No. This time you're the one who draws the line for us.

259
30:03.800 --> 30:05.470
Then at the school event this year,

260
30:08.800 --> 30:10.330
watch the fireworks with me.

261
31:00.730 --> 31:02.270
Not going back to sleep?

262
31:03.170 --> 31:04.800
I can't sleep.

263
31:07.400 --> 31:08.770
Want to sleep together, then?

264
31:09.930 --> 31:11.430
You already sleep at my place, don't you?

265
32:12.430 --> 32:14.000
You okay?

266
32:17.900 --> 32:20.930
And are you okay, Din?

267
32:28.130 --> 32:29.370
Okay.

268
32:30.070 --> 32:32.030
I talked to Fuen.

269
32:36.030 --> 32:38.130
At least I didn't lose a friend.

270
32:42.230 --> 32:45.170
But taking the person my friend likes,

271
32:47.870 --> 32:49.870
I just can't do it.

272
32:50.530 --> 32:51.670
Exactly.

273
32:52.900 --> 32:57.130
I'm... not good at taking someone out of another person's heart either.

274
33:00.570 --> 33:03.500
Letting go yourself is much easier, Din.

275
33:05.200 --> 33:07.270
And besides, my dad taught me that

276
33:07.630 --> 33:10.130
he raised me with love

277
33:12.170 --> 33:13.800
and happiness.

278
33:14.400 --> 33:18.670
So I must never let anyone make me sad.

279
33:27.930 --> 33:29.800
Oh, Din.

280
33:32.700 --> 33:35.870
I'd like to get your contact.

281
33:39.100 --> 33:42.800
I want to pay you back for saving me when I fell in the water.

282
33:43.470 --> 33:45.570
No need. It was just my job.

283
33:45.570 --> 33:49.470
Job or not, I feel like I have to...

284
33:50.270 --> 33:52.070
give you something back.

285
33:54.800 --> 33:57.030
At least let me take you out for a meal, Din.

286
33:58.930 --> 34:01.330
Why do you like taking people out to eat so much?

287
34:06.870 --> 34:09.670
Then whenever I'm hungry,

288
34:10.429 --> 34:12.130
I'll just get Star's contact from someone else.

289
34:12.600 --> 34:14.699
Why would you get it from someone else?

290
34:14.699 --> 34:16.929
Why not just ask me right now?

291
34:17.969 --> 34:20.730
If you got it from someone else, or my friends found out,

292
34:21.929 --> 34:24.429
my contact doesn't come that easy, Din.

293
34:25.070 --> 34:25.870
Hey.

294
34:25.870 --> 34:27.800
Mine doesn't come easy either.

295
34:28.130 --> 34:30.170
People at school sell mine.

296
34:30.170 --> 34:31.230
For good money.

297
34:31.600 --> 34:35.170
But mine is very expensive, Din.

298
34:35.929 --> 34:37.830
I think I can afford it.

299
34:37.830 --> 34:40.600
Then it's up to you.

300
34:42.230 --> 34:44.600
Consider yourself warned.

301
35:04.230 --> 35:07.130
Est, Jay, and Chemi.

302
35:08.730 --> 35:10.270
Go ahead, go ahead.

303
35:13.200 --> 35:15.230
Hey, there they are.

304
35:15.570 --> 35:18.430
That's all of M.5, then.

305
35:18.900 --> 35:20.500
See you, guys.

306
35:20.500 --> 35:22.100
See you up there.

307
35:23.470 --> 35:25.870
The rest of them... check them in.

308
35:26.930 --> 35:28.470
Check them all.

309
35:28.470 --> 35:29.970
Is anyone hiding around here?

310
35:30.200 --> 35:31.830
No one's hiding at this point.

311
35:31.830 --> 35:33.000
They all want to go home.

312
35:34.400 --> 35:35.700
Just Aof left...

313
35:40.500 --> 35:42.300
All of M.6 is here.

314
35:45.900 --> 35:47.300
Okay. / All present.

315
35:47.300 --> 35:48.370
Right. / All present, then.

316
36:16.870 --> 36:18.800
I know you're not asleep.

317
36:20.900 --> 36:22.630
Are you really going to let him go?

318
36:26.100 --> 36:29.570
I don't know what to do next.

319
36:30.400 --> 36:34.170
My question wasn't as hard as you made it out to be, was it?

320
36:36.530 --> 36:38.930
I've tried to understand him, but

321
36:40.070 --> 36:41.800
I still don't get him.

322
36:44.070 --> 36:46.370
Then keep your distance for a while.

323
36:47.100 --> 36:48.630
Stick with us.

324
36:51.200 --> 36:52.700
Don't you guys leave me.

325
36:54.070 --> 36:57.600
Even if I'm being an idiot, don't you dare leave me.

326
36:58.570 --> 37:00.770
Yeah, no one's leaving you.

327
37:00.770 --> 37:02.870
If we did, no one else would take you.

328
37:03.530 --> 37:06.170
But I want to be with you. All of you.

329
37:06.170 --> 37:07.170
Oh.

330
37:08.670 --> 37:11.070
You could just leave me and Zac alone together.

331
37:11.730 --> 37:14.200
And leave me with Est? No thanks.

332
37:16.300 --> 37:20.630
Then let's keep being this gloriously pointless little squad.

333
37:20.630 --> 37:21.970
Sounds good, man.

334
37:43.100 --> 37:46.230
Hey, now that camp's over,

335
37:46.230 --> 37:51.000
I think we should start talking about Thapfah Countdown.

336
37:51.000 --> 37:55.500
No problem. I've already got some of the details ready.

337
37:55.500 --> 37:58.900
By the way, do you want it open to outsiders or students only?

338
37:59.430 --> 38:01.030
Open to outsiders, like every year.

339
38:01.030 --> 38:03.030
Ticket price stays the same.

340
38:03.030 --> 38:04.630
As for the performances,

341
38:04.630 --> 38:06.670
I think each class should pitch

342
38:06.670 --> 38:08.070
what they want to do,

343
38:08.600 --> 38:10.030
and we'll see where we can support them.

344
38:10.030 --> 38:12.200
I'll handle the booths myself.

345
38:12.630 --> 38:14.500
I think we can use last year's vendor.

346
38:15.000 --> 38:16.630
All good. We'll talk later.

347
38:17.100 --> 38:19.800
We've still got a month or so before the event.

348
38:26.600 --> 38:27.870
Let's go!

349
38:41.070 --> 38:41.870
Really, Dad?

350
38:42.970 --> 38:44.670
Oh, Dad, Dad, hold on.

351
38:44.670 --> 38:46.730
I think our son's back, Dad.

352
38:48.970 --> 38:51.730
Why didn't you tell us you were coming? I'd have come to get you.

353
38:51.730 --> 38:52.730
It's fine, Mom.

354
38:52.730 --> 38:54.230
Getting a ride on the app is easier.

355
38:54.230 --> 38:55.770
You'd just get stuck in traffic.

356
38:55.770 --> 38:56.870
So, did you have fun?

357
38:57.530 --> 38:59.000
Don't tell it yet, don't tell it.

358
38:59.000 --> 39:00.330
Your dad's right here. Come on.

359
39:00.330 --> 39:01.500
Dad's calling?

360
39:02.230 --> 39:03.500
Darling, our son's home.

361
39:03.500 --> 39:05.030
Hi, Dad.

362
39:05.030 --> 39:08.300
It was great, and the seniors took really good care of me.

363
39:08.300 --> 39:11.570
My brother came along too, but he stuck with Fuen as usual.

364
39:12.130 --> 39:12.930
Really?

365
39:12.930 --> 39:16.630
So, have you won Fuen over yet?

366
39:19.600 --> 39:23.200
Not yet, but I'm making progress.

367
39:23.200 --> 39:25.100
I already told Fuen how I feel.

368
39:26.030 --> 39:27.270
Really, son?

369
39:27.900 --> 39:28.770
Yes. / And?

370
39:28.770 --> 39:30.600
Should I start saving for the dowry?

371
39:32.700 --> 39:34.930
Whoa, amazing, bro.

372
39:34.930 --> 39:37.270
Hey, what happened, what happened?

373
39:37.270 --> 39:40.700
Then I'll clear my schedule and book tickets back to Thailand.

374
39:40.700 --> 39:43.300
Slow down, Dad.

375
39:44.000 --> 39:48.230
I told Fuen, but he still needs time to think.

376
39:50.100 --> 39:53.900
But he didn't seem like he'd turn you down, did he?

377
39:56.470 --> 39:59.900
I'm not bracing myself anymore. I'm all in.

378
40:00.600 --> 40:03.130
I don't know about that yet, Dad, Mom.

379
40:05.170 --> 40:07.230
I guess time will tell.

380
40:10.800 --> 40:12.930
If two people are really meant for each other,

381
40:12.930 --> 40:15.470
they'll always find their way back to each other.

382
40:19.270 --> 40:22.200
And how do you know you're meant for each other?

383
40:23.130 --> 40:24.630
If having you in his life

384
40:25.230 --> 40:29.600
makes him safer, better off and happier,

385
40:30.730 --> 40:33.200
then he'll never let you go.

386
40:39.570 --> 40:40.900
In that case...

387
40:42.400 --> 40:44.200
I'm pretty confident that...

388
40:44.600 --> 40:47.770
I am a good thing in Fuen's life.

389
40:48.570 --> 40:51.500
Whoa, bro, a little overconfident?

390
40:52.070 --> 40:53.500
Hey. / Yes?

391
40:55.330 --> 41:00.800
Honestly, no, because I think Fuen

392
41:00.800 --> 41:04.330
definitely won't find a better friend than me.

393
41:07.670 --> 41:10.070
That's the confidence, son.

394
41:10.770 --> 41:12.430
But let me tell you, I've seen plenty of these.

395
41:12.430 --> 41:14.370
The ones who plan too much

396
41:14.800 --> 41:16.400
are the ones who end up not making it.

397
41:17.470 --> 41:19.170
Mom. Mom.

398
41:19.600 --> 41:22.470
Let's just say I

399
41:22.470 --> 41:23.570
definitely won't slip up.

400
41:24.330 --> 41:26.600
And none of you need to worry about me.

401
41:27.030 --> 41:29.600
What you should worry about

402
41:29.600 --> 41:33.670
is your youngest son right here.

403
41:33.670 --> 41:37.670
His life's been quite the mess lately.

404
41:38.600 --> 41:42.630
What is it, son? What's going on? Why didn't you tell me?

405
41:42.630 --> 41:44.100
Oh, come on, bro.

406
41:44.370 --> 41:45.730
Doing this to your little brother.

407
41:45.730 --> 41:47.030
Hey. / Yes?

408
41:48.230 --> 41:50.030
Are you telling them or not?

409
41:51.370 --> 41:52.600
If you don't, I will.

410
41:52.600 --> 41:53.870
Fine, I'll tell them.

411
41:56.900 --> 42:00.730
But could you go somewhere else? Go up to your room. I'll tell them myself.

412
42:00.730 --> 42:05.130
No, I happen to want the details.

413
42:06.900 --> 42:07.700
Out with it.

414
42:09.830 --> 42:10.630
Okay.

415
42:25.700 --> 42:30.370
♪ When you turn to me, I can't hold your gaze for long ♪

416
42:30.370 --> 42:36.070
♪ I carry it into my dreams each night, but I can't do a thing about it ♪

417
42:36.070 --> 42:41.370
♪ Every look you send my way makes my heart shake even more ♪

418
42:41.370 --> 42:46.370
♪ One slip and I'm imagining things ♪

419
42:46.370 --> 42:52.200
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day ♪

420
42:52.200 --> 42:56.870
♪ My heart can't take it ♪

421
43:05.000 --> 43:10.370
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

422
43:10.370 --> 43:15.970
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

423
43:15.970 --> 43:21.530
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

424
43:21.530 --> 43:26.200
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

425
43:38.570 --> 43:43.470
♪ Afraid that if I say it, you'll never look at me the same ♪

426
43:43.470 --> 43:49.170
♪ Afraid that one day what we have will break ♪

427
43:49.170 --> 43:54.800
♪ Should I say it, or just let it stay a dream ♪

428
43:54.800 --> 43:59.470
♪ One slip and I'm imagining things ♪

429
43:59.470 --> 44:05.300
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day ♪

430
44:05.300 --> 44:08.000
♪ My heart can't take it ♪

431
44:08.530 --> 44:12.470
"Sleep well. See you tomorrow."

432
44:12.470 --> 44:14.730
"Sleep well."

433
44:15.770 --> 44:21.130
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

434
44:21.130 --> 44:26.730
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

435
44:26.730 --> 44:32.300
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

436
44:32.300 --> 44:36.970
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

437
44:44.100 --> 44:46.400
"Star, do you have some time tomorrow?"

438
44:46.400 --> 44:48.400
"There's something I want to talk about."

439
45:05.400 --> 45:07.930
I'm sorry, Star.

440
45:09.170 --> 45:11.770
I really can't help you anymore, Star.

441
45:13.330 --> 45:15.870
It's okay. I understand.

442
45:17.130 --> 45:20.330
And you don't need to think about me anymore, Fuen.

443
45:23.130 --> 45:25.970
I'm really okay now.

444
45:25.970 --> 45:28.500
Okay. Really, Star?

445
45:28.500 --> 45:29.900
Really.

446
45:32.300 --> 45:35.030
There's one more thing I want to ask you, Star.

447
45:36.170 --> 45:37.600
What is it?

448
45:38.770 --> 45:39.930
That camera.

449
45:41.700 --> 45:44.270
Can I buy it from you?

450
45:49.100 --> 45:50.200
Sure.

451
45:50.200 --> 45:53.030
Let's call it the end of our deal.

452
45:55.100 --> 45:55.900
Thanks.

453
45:56.200 --> 45:57.200
But...

454
45:57.430 --> 46:00.670
now that we're like brothers, it's full price.

455
46:00.670 --> 46:02.830
No discount.

456
46:02.830 --> 46:04.200
Star.

457
46:05.200 --> 46:07.430
Your family's rich already.

458
46:07.430 --> 46:10.230
Can't you give me a discount? Come on.

459
46:10.230 --> 46:11.500
Do you want it or not?

460
46:11.500 --> 46:12.630
I'll take it.

461
46:13.770 --> 46:15.800
I'll transfer the money.

462
46:15.800 --> 46:17.300
Same account.

463
46:17.300 --> 46:18.230
Yes, dear.

464
46:30.730 --> 46:32.370
Transfer late and I'm keeping it.

465
46:32.370 --> 46:34.170
Transferring now.

466
46:42.930 --> 46:45.330
I think the stage play this year looks really interesting.

467
46:45.330 --> 46:48.500
And with a good script to work with, it'd be even more fun.

468
46:50.270 --> 46:51.700
I agree.

469
46:51.700 --> 46:55.170
I heard our school has a famous novelist, right?

470
46:55.170 --> 46:57.300
Who? I've never heard of them.

471
46:57.730 --> 47:01.770
If I remember right, his name's Kim, M.5.

472
47:01.770 --> 47:04.670
But he doesn't show his face on social media.

473
47:04.670 --> 47:06.970
Super mysterious.

474
47:08.000 --> 47:12.030
I don't know who he is either. We'd have to go find out.

475
47:13.130 --> 47:14.230
I'll leave that to you, then.

476
47:15.070 --> 47:17.430
This year's theme is carnival, right?

477
47:19.030 --> 47:21.330
Since this is our last year,

478
47:22.100 --> 47:24.200
let's go all out.

479
47:24.830 --> 47:28.200
Then tell everyone: no limits on ideas this year.

480
47:28.200 --> 47:30.330
Just make it creative and fun.

481
47:30.700 --> 47:31.730
Let's do it.

482
47:32.430 --> 47:33.930
Oh, Din.

483
47:33.930 --> 47:35.430
Have you talked to Star yet?

484
47:35.830 --> 47:38.230
About having him do PR with Tonnam.

485
47:39.000 --> 47:41.100
Oh, I totally forgot. Thanks for the reminder.

486
47:41.100 --> 47:43.600
So why don't you just call him?

487
47:44.130 --> 47:45.430
I don't have his contact.

488
47:45.430 --> 47:47.070
And why not?

489
47:48.900 --> 47:50.070
I never asked.

490
47:50.070 --> 47:51.770
And why didn't you ask?

491
47:53.370 --> 47:55.300
Why are you two talking in unison?

492
47:55.300 --> 47:57.230
All right, all right, I'll go now.

493
47:59.300 --> 48:00.700
Oh, Din.

494
48:04.800 --> 48:05.700
No contact.

495
48:56.930 --> 48:59.370
Say whatever it is.

496
49:10.630 --> 49:13.530
I know this is the camera you wanted,

497
49:15.130 --> 49:18.130
and you can't buy it anywhere anymore.

498
49:26.570 --> 49:29.370
So I bought it off Star.

499
49:29.370 --> 49:32.630
Which means this camera is mine now.

500
49:47.900 --> 49:50.370
I bought it for you on purpose.

501
49:53.830 --> 49:57.000
Please take it.

502
50:02.070 --> 50:04.200
I'm sorry.

503
50:37.970 --> 50:40.270
Anything you buy for me on purpose,

504
50:42.670 --> 50:44.630
I want all of it.

505
52:10.400 --> 52:13.430
You're really not mad at me anymore?

506
52:20.600 --> 52:22.330
In the end, if you understand me,

507
52:22.330 --> 52:24.030
I'm not mad at you.

508
52:28.470 --> 52:31.330
Your heart is pounding right now.

509
52:31.330 --> 52:32.530
I like it.

510
52:36.730 --> 52:39.600
You said you'd give me space and time.

511
52:40.570 --> 52:45.800
I am. Why... not enough?

512
52:47.370 --> 52:50.300
Oh, really? That's all I get?

513
53:43.230 --> 53:49.400
The first photo on this camera, let it be you and me.

514
53:53.470 --> 53:56.770
You already took it. Why ask?

515
54:32.500 --> 54:35.130
I waited so long for you, my baby.

516
54:36.330 --> 54:38.800
So long for someone to bring you to me.

517
54:41.100 --> 54:43.230
I brought him, didn't I?

518
54:46.070 --> 54:47.600
Sorry it took a while.

519
55:11.770 --> 55:15.700
Everyone, turn to page 38.

520
55:29.100 --> 55:30.600
Excuse me, teacher. / Oh, Din.

521
55:30.870 --> 55:33.030
Does the student council need to talk to the juniors today?

522
55:33.030 --> 55:34.170
It's something important.

523
55:34.170 --> 55:36.300
So could I borrow a moment of your time?

524
55:36.300 --> 55:37.600
Sure, sure, go ahead.

525
55:51.000 --> 55:52.570
Hey, juniors.

526
55:57.830 --> 56:00.030
Could I get Star's contact?

527
56:02.870 --> 56:04.130
No.

528
56:12.530 --> 56:14.730
"I usually sell my LINE to girls for 500 each. (Din)"

529
56:14.730 --> 56:16.500
"Huh. Mine goes for 1,000. (Star)"

530
56:17.100 --> 56:21.600
"I'm waiting for the day you're my boyfriend."

531
56:22.070 --> 56:24.100
"So how much longer are you going to play hard to get? (Jay)"

532
56:24.100 --> 56:26.130
"Trust me, Aof's going to figure out he still likes him. Just look at his eyes. (Zac)"

533
56:26.800 --> 56:28.870
Today I have an announcement for everyone

534
56:28.870 --> 56:30.830
about our school event this year.

535
56:30.830 --> 56:33.470
The event everyone's been waiting for: Thapfah Countdown.

536
56:33.470 --> 56:36.230
Don't forget to invite that special someone, or the one you've got your eye on,

537
56:36.230 --> 56:37.600
well in advance.

538
56:37.600 --> 56:38.730
Mission's here, right?

539
56:38.730 --> 56:39.530
Easier than you'd think.

540
56:39.530 --> 56:40.330
If there's ever a day you can't take it, Din,

541
56:40.330 --> 56:42.200
you have to stop. / I promise.

542
56:42.200 --> 56:43.470
I'm jealous of you and Chemi.

543
56:43.470 --> 56:45.000
You promised you wouldn't tell anyone.

544
56:45.000 --> 56:47.230
You didn't do a single thing you said you would.

545
56:47.770 --> 56:49.770
I don't know what I'm waiting for either.

546
56:50.370 --> 56:53.400
You two are so close. Don't ever break up.

547
56:53.400 --> 56:54.970
Let me win you over first.
